\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/incorrect-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectText\">Incorrect</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>A curve is closed if its terminal point coincides with its initial point. So, a curve whose terminal point does not coincide with its initial point is not closed. </p>\n<p>Of the given options, the only one that is not a closed curve is the following:</p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-98319-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-98319-e-0\"></div></div></div>",
